msgid "Max print height"
msgstr "Max print height"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1075
msgid "Set this to the maximum height that can be reached by your extruder while printing."
msgstr "Set this to the maximum height that can be reached by your extruder while printing."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1083
msgid "Allow exceeding max height"
msgstr "Allow exceeding max height"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1084
msgid ""
"By default, G-code export is blocked when any generated Z movement, including Z offset, Z-hop or "
"lift, and custom G-code, exceeds Max print height. Enable this option to allow such G-code to be "
"exported. This does not allow models taller than Max print height and does not change the "
"printer's physical limits. Enable it only if the printer can safely execute movements beyond the "
"configured maximum height."
msgstr ""
"By default, G-code export is blocked when any generated Z movement, including Z offset, Z-hop or "
"lift, and custom G-code, exceeds Max print height. Enable this option to allow such G-code to be "
"exported. This does not allow models taller than Max print height and does not change the "
"printer's physical limits. Enable it only if the printer can safely execute movements beyond the "
"configured maximum height."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1091
msgid "Hostname, IP or URL"
msgstr "Hostname, IP or URL"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1092
msgid ""
"Slic3r can upload G-code files to a printer host. This field should contain the hostname, IP "
"address or URL of the printer host instance. Print host behind HAProxy with basic auth enabled "
"can be accessed by putting the user name and password into the URL in the following format: "
"https://username:password@your-octopi-address/"
msgstr ""
"Slic3r can upload G-code files to a printer host. This field should contain the hostname, IP "
"address or URL of the printer host instance. Print host behind HAProxy with basic auth enabled "
"can be accessed by putting the user name and password into the URL in the following format: "
"https://username:password@your-octopi-address/"

