#. TRN PrintSettings : "Dynamic overhang speed"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1497
msgid ""
"Overhang size is expressed as a percentage of overlap of the extrusion with the previous layer: "
"100% would be full overlap (no overhang), while 0% represents full overhang (floating extrusion, "
"bridge). Speeds for overhang sizes in between are calculated via linear interpolation. If set as "
"percentage, the speed is calculated over the external perimeter speed. Note that the speeds "
"generated to gcode will never exceed the max volumetric speed value."
msgstr ""
"Overhang size is expressed as a percentage of overlap of the extrusion with the previous layer: "
"100% would be full overlap (no overhang), while 0% represents full overhang (floating extrusion, "
"bridge). Speeds for overhang sizes in between are calculated via linear interpolation. If set as "
"percentage, the speed is calculated over the external perimeter speed. Note that the speeds "
"generated to gcode will never exceed the max volumetric speed value."

