#: src/slic3r/GUI/Preferences.cpp:878 src/slic3r/GUI/Tab.cpp:1631 src/slic3r/GUI/Tab.cpp:1640
msgid "None"
msgstr "None"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3333
msgid "Outside walls"
msgstr "Outside walls"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3334
msgid "All walls"
msgstr "All walls"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3340
msgid "Fuzzy skin thickness"
msgstr "Fuzzy skin thickness"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3342
msgid ""
"The maximum distance that each skin point can be offset (both ways), measured perpendicular to "
"the perimeter wall."
msgstr ""
"The maximum distance that each skin point can be offset (both ways), measured perpendicular to "
"the perimeter wall."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3350
msgid "Fuzzy skin point distance"
msgstr "Fuzzy skin point distance"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3352
msgid ""
"Perimeters will be split into multiple segments by inserting Fuzzy skin points. Lowering the "
"Fuzzy skin point distance will increase the number of randomly offset points on the perimeter "
"wall."
msgstr ""
"Perimeters will be split into multiple segments by inserting Fuzzy skin points. Lowering the "
"Fuzzy skin point distance will increase the number of randomly offset points on the perimeter "
"wall."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3360
msgid "Fill gaps"
msgstr "Fill gaps"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3362
msgid "Enables filling of gaps between perimeters and between the inner most perimeters and infill."
msgstr ""
"Enables filling of gaps between perimeters and between the inner most perimeters and infill."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3369
msgid ""
"Speed for filling small gaps using short zigzag moves. Keep this reasonably low to avoid too much "
"shaking and resonance issues. Set zero to disable gaps filling."
msgstr ""
"Speed for filling small gaps using short zigzag moves. Keep this reasonably low to avoid too much "
"shaking and resonance issues. Set zero to disable gaps filling."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3377
msgid "Verbose G-code"
msgstr "Verbose G-code"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3378
msgid ""
"Enable this to get a commented G-code file, with each line explained by a descriptive text. If "
"you print from SD card, the additional weight of the file could make your firmware slow down."
msgstr ""
"Enable this to get a commented G-code file, with each line explained by a descriptive text. If "
"you print from SD card, the additional weight of the file could make your firmware slow down."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3385
msgid "G-code flavor"
msgstr "G-code flavor"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3386
msgid ""
"Some G/M-code commands, including temperature control and others, are not universal. Set this "
"option to your printer's firmware to get a compatible output. The \"No extrusion\" flavor "
"prevents PrusaSlicer from exporting any extrusion value at all."
msgstr ""
"Some G/M-code commands, including temperature control and others, are not universal. Set this "
"option to your printer's firmware to get a compatible output. The \"No extrusion\" flavor "
"prevents PrusaSlicer from exporting any extrusion value at all."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3402
msgid "No extrusion"
msgstr "No extrusion"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3408
msgid "Label objects"
msgstr "Label objects"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3409
msgid ""
"Selects whether labels should be exported at object boundaries and in what format.\n"
"OctoPrint = comments to be consumed by OctoPrint CancelObject plugin.\n"
"Firmware = firmware specific G-code (it will be chosen based on firmware flavor and it can end up "
"to be empty).\n"
"\n"
"This settings is NOT compatible with Single Extruder Multi Material setup and Wipe into Object / "
"Wipe into Infill."
msgstr ""
"Selects whether labels should be exported at object boundaries and in what format.\n"
"OctoPrint = comments to be consumed by OctoPrint CancelObject plugin.\n"
"Firmware = firmware specific G-code (it will be chosen based on firmware flavor and it can end up "
"to be empty).\n"
"\n"
"This settings is NOT compatible with Single Extruder Multi Material setup and Wipe into Object / "
"Wipe into Infill."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3416
msgid "OctoPrint comments"
msgstr "OctoPrint comments"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3417
msgid "Firmware-specific"
msgstr "Firmware-specific"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3423
msgid "G-code substitutions"
msgstr "G-code substitutions"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3424
msgid "Find / replace patterns in G-code lines and substitute them."
msgstr "Find / replace patterns in G-code lines and substitute them."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3429
msgid "Use legacy header"
msgstr "Use legacy header"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3430
msgid "If enabled, the G-code header uses \"PrusaSlicer\" instead of the current application name."
msgstr "If enabled, the G-code header uses \"PrusaSlicer\" instead of the current application name."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3435
msgid "High extruder current on material swap"
msgstr "High extruder current on material swap"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3436
msgid ""
"It may be beneficial to increase the extruder motor current during the material exchange sequence "
"to allow for rapid ramming feed rates and to overcome resistance when loading a material with an "
"ugly shaped tip."
msgstr ""
"It may be beneficial to increase the extruder motor current during the material exchange sequence "
"to allow for rapid ramming feed rates and to overcome resistance when loading a material with an "
"ugly shaped tip."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3444
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for infill. Set zero to disable acceleration "
"control for infill."
msgstr ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for infill. Set zero to disable acceleration "
"control for infill."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3453
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for solid infill. Set zero to use the value for "
"infill."
msgstr ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for solid infill. Set zero to use the value for "
"infill."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3462
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for top solid infill. Set zero to use the value "
"for solid infill."
msgstr ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for top solid infill. Set zero to use the value "
"for solid infill."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3471
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for wipe tower. Set zero to disable acceleration "
"control for the wipe tower."
msgstr ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for wipe tower. Set zero to disable acceleration "
"control for the wipe tower."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3479 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6116
#: src/slic3r/GUI/GCodeViewer.cpp:1166 src/slic3r/GUI/GCodeViewer.cpp:4240
#: src/slic3r/GUI/GCodeViewer.cpp:4778 src/slic3r/GUI/Sidebar.cpp:677 src/slic3r/GUI/Sidebar.cpp:693
msgid "Travel"
msgstr "Travel"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3480
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for travel moves. Set zero to disable acceleration "
"control for travel."
msgstr ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for travel moves. Set zero to disable acceleration "
"control for travel."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3488
msgid "Travel short distance acceleration"
msgstr "Travel short distance acceleration"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3489
msgid ""
"Acceleration used for short travel moves. Short travel distance is determined by the "
"retract_before_travel setting."
msgstr ""
"Acceleration used for short travel moves. Short travel distance is determined by the "
"retract_before_travel setting."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3496
msgid "Combine infill every"
msgstr "Combine infill every"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3498
msgid ""
"This feature allows to combine infill and speed up your print by extruding thicker infill layers "
"while preserving thin perimeters, thus accuracy."
msgstr ""
"This feature allows to combine infill and speed up your print by extruding thicker infill layers "
"while preserving thin perimeters, thus accuracy."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3501
msgid "Combine infill every n layers"
msgstr "Combine infill every n layers"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3507
msgid "Length of the infill anchor"
msgstr "Length of the infill anchor"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3509
msgid ""
"Connect an infill line to an internal perimeter with a short segment of an additional perimeter. "
"If expressed as percentage (example: 15%) it is calculated over infill extrusion width. "
"PrusaSlicer tries to connect two close infill lines to a short perimeter segment. If no such "
"perimeter segment shorter than infill_anchor_max is found, the infill line is connected to a "
"perimeter segment at just one side and the length of the perimeter segment taken is limited to "
"this parameter, but no longer than anchor_length_max. Set this parameter to zero to disable "
"anchoring perimeters connected to a single infill line."
msgstr ""
"Connect an infill line to an internal perimeter with a short segment of an additional perimeter. "
"If expressed as percentage (example: 15%) it is calculated over infill extrusion width. "
"PrusaSlicer tries to connect two close infill lines to a short perimeter segment. If no such "
"perimeter segment shorter than infill_anchor_max is found, the infill line is connected to a "
"perimeter segment at just one side and the length of the perimeter segment taken is limited to "
"this parameter, but no longer than anchor_length_max. Set this parameter to zero to disable "
"anchoring perimeters connected to a single infill line."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3519
msgid "0 (no open anchors)"
msgstr "0 (no open anchors)"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3520 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3543
msgid "1 mm"
msgstr "1 mm"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3521 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3544
msgid "2 mm"
msgstr "2 mm"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3522 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3545
msgid "5 mm"
msgstr "5 mm"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3523 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3546
msgid "10 mm"
msgstr "10 mm"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3524 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3547
msgid "1000 (unlimited)"
msgstr "1000 (unlimited)"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3530
msgid "Maximum length of the infill anchor"
msgstr "Maximum length of the infill anchor"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3532
msgid ""
"Connect an infill line to an internal perimeter with a short segment of an additional perimeter. "
"If expressed as percentage (example: 15%) it is calculated over infill extrusion width. "
"PrusaSlicer tries to connect two close infill lines to a short perimeter segment. If no such "
"perimeter segment shorter than this parameter is found, the infill line is connected to a "
"perimeter segment at just one side and the length of the perimeter segment taken is limited to "
"infill_anchor, but no longer than this parameter. Set this parameter to zero to disable anchoring."
msgstr ""
"Connect an infill line to an internal perimeter with a short segment of an additional perimeter. "
"If expressed as percentage (example: 15%) it is calculated over infill extrusion width. "
"PrusaSlicer tries to connect two close infill lines to a short perimeter segment. If no such "
"perimeter segment shorter than this parameter is found, the infill line is connected to a "
"perimeter segment at just one side and the length of the perimeter segment taken is limited to "
"infill_anchor, but no longer than this parameter. Set this parameter to zero to disable anchoring."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3542
msgid "0 (not anchored)"
msgstr "0 (not anchored)"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3553
msgid "Infill extruder"
msgstr "Infill extruder"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3555
msgid "The tool to use when printing infill. T0 is the first extruder."
msgstr "The tool to use when printing infill. T0 is the first extruder."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3563
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill. If left zero, default "
"extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. You may want "
"to use fatter extrudates to speed up the infill and make your parts stronger. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill. If left zero, default "
"extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. You may want "
"to use fatter extrudates to speed up the infill and make your parts stronger. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3576
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3588
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for bridge infill. If left zero, "
"bridge infill width is derived from bridge flow ratio and nozzle diameter. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for bridge infill. If left zero, "
"bridge infill width is derived from bridge flow ratio and nozzle diameter. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3600
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based bridge infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage "
"values."
msgstr ""
"Base for percentage-based bridge infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage "
"values."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3610
msgid "Infill before perimeters"
msgstr "Infill before perimeters"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3611
msgid "This option will switch the print order of perimeters and infill, making the latter first."
msgstr "This option will switch the print order of perimeters and infill, making the latter first."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3625
msgid "Infill/perimeters overlap"
msgstr "Infill/perimeters overlap"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3627
msgid ""
"This setting applies an additional overlap between infill and perimeters for better bonding. "
"Theoretically this shouldn't be needed, but backlash might cause gaps. If expressed as percentage "
"(example: 15%) it is calculated over perimeter extrusion width."
msgstr ""
"This setting applies an additional overlap between infill and perimeters for better bonding. "
"Theoretically this shouldn't be needed, but backlash might cause gaps. If expressed as percentage "
"(example: 15%) it is calculated over perimeter extrusion width."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3638
msgid "Speed for printing the internal fill. Set to zero for auto."
msgstr "Speed for printing the internal fill. Set to zero for auto."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3646
msgid "Inherits profile"
msgstr "Inherits profile"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3647
msgid "Name of the profile, from which this profile inherits."
msgstr "Name of the profile, from which this profile inherits."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3660
msgid "Interface shells"
msgstr "Interface shells"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3661
msgid ""
"Force the generation of solid shells between adjacent materials/volumes. Useful for multi-"
"extruder prints with translucent materials or manual soluble support material."
msgstr ""
"Force the generation of solid shells between adjacent materials/volumes. Useful for multi-"
"extruder prints with translucent materials or manual soluble support material."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3669
msgid "Maximum width of a segmented region"
msgstr "Maximum width of a segmented region"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3670
msgid "Maximum width of a segmented region. Zero disables this feature."
msgstr "Maximum width of a segmented region. Zero disables this feature."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3671 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3682
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4636 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4646
msgid "mm (zero to disable)"
msgstr "mm (zero to disable)"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3678
msgid "Interlocking depth of a segmented region"
msgstr "Interlocking depth of a segmented region"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3679
msgid ""
"Interlocking depth of a segmented region. It will be ignored if "
"\"mmu_segmented_region_max_width\" is zero or if \"mmu_segmented_region_interlocking_depth\"is "
"bigger then \"mmu_segmented_region_max_width\". Zero disables this feature."
msgstr ""
"Interlocking depth of a segmented region. It will be ignored if "
"\"mmu_segmented_region_max_width\" is zero or if \"mmu_segmented_region_interlocking_depth\"is "
"bigger then \"mmu_segmented_region_max_width\". Zero disables this feature."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3689
msgid "Enable ironing"
msgstr "Enable ironing"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3690
msgid "Enable ironing of the top layers with the hot print head for smooth surface"
msgstr "Enable ironing of the top layers with the hot print head for smooth surface"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3696
msgid "Use beam interlocking"
msgstr "Use beam interlocking"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3697
msgid ""
"Generate interlocking beam structure at the locations where different materials touch. This "
"improves the adhesion between materials, especially models printed in different materials."
msgstr ""
"Generate interlocking beam structure at the locations where different materials touch. This "
"improves the adhesion between materials, especially models printed in different materials."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3703
msgid "Interlocking beam width"
msgstr "Interlocking beam width"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3704
msgid "The width of the interlocking structure beams."
msgstr "The width of the interlocking structure beams."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3712
msgid "Interlocking direction"
msgstr "Interlocking direction"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3713
msgid "Orientation of interlocking beams."
msgstr "Orientation of interlocking beams."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3722
msgid "Interlocking beam layers"
msgstr "Interlocking beam layers"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3723
msgid ""
"The height of the beams of the interlocking structure, measured in number of layers. Less layers "
"is stronger, but more prone to defects."
msgstr ""
"The height of the beams of the interlocking structure, measured in number of layers. Less layers "
"is stronger, but more prone to defects."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3730
msgid "Interlocking depth"
msgstr "Interlocking depth"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3731
msgid ""
"The distance from the boundary between materials to generate interlocking structure, measured in "
"cells. Too few cells will result in poor adhesion."
msgstr ""
"The distance from the boundary between materials to generate interlocking structure, measured in "
"cells. Too few cells will result in poor adhesion."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3738
msgid "Interlocking boundary avoidance"
msgstr "Interlocking boundary avoidance"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3739
msgid ""
"The distance from the outside of a model where interlocking structures will not be generated, "
"measured in cells."
msgstr ""
"The distance from the outside of a model where interlocking structures will not be generated, "
"measured in cells."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3746 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3748
msgid "Ironing type"
msgstr "Ironing type"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3750
msgid "Painted"
msgstr "Painted"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3751
msgid "Topmost"
msgstr "Topmost"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3752
msgid "All solid"
msgstr "All solid"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3758
msgid "Ironing on support interface top"
msgstr "Ironing on support interface top"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3760
msgid ""
"Iron the top contact surfaces of non-raft support interfaces in addition to the selected object "
"ironing type."
msgstr ""
"Iron the top contact surfaces of non-raft support interfaces in addition to the selected object "
"ironing type."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3771
msgid "Ironing angle"
msgstr "Ironing angle"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3773
msgid ""
"Base angle for ironing movements. Set to 0 to use the automatic angle derived from the infill "
"angle."
msgstr ""
"Base angle for ironing movements. Set to 0 to use the automatic angle derived from the infill "
"angle."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3782
msgid "Flow rate"
msgstr "Flow rate"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3784
msgid "Percent of a flow rate relative to object's normal layer height."
msgstr "Percent of a flow rate relative to object's normal layer height."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3792
msgid "Spacing between ironing passes"
msgstr "Spacing between ironing passes"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3794
msgid "Distance between ironing lines"
msgstr "Distance between ironing lines"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3811
msgid ""
"This custom code is inserted at every layer change, right after the Z move and before the "
"extruder moves to the first layer point. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"Slic3r settings as well as [layer_num] and [layer_z]."
msgstr ""
"This custom code is inserted at every layer change, right after the Z move and before the "
"extruder moves to the first layer point. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"Slic3r settings as well as [layer_num] and [layer_z]."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3822
msgid "Supports remaining times"
msgstr "Supports remaining times"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3823
msgid ""
"Emit M73 P[percent printed] R[remaining time in minutes] at 1 minute intervals into the G-code to "
"let the firmware show accurate remaining time. As of now only the Prusa i3 MK3 firmware "
"recognizes M73. Also the i3 MK3 firmware supports M73 Qxx Sxx for the silent mode."
msgstr ""
"Emit M73 P[percent printed] R[remaining time in minutes] at 1 minute intervals into the G-code to "
"let the firmware show accurate remaining time. As of now only the Prusa i3 MK3 firmware "
"recognizes M73. Also the i3 MK3 firmware supports M73 Qxx Sxx for the silent mode."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3831
msgid "Supports stealth mode"
msgstr "Supports stealth mode"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3832
msgid "The firmware supports stealth mode"
msgstr "The firmware supports stealth mode"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3837
msgid "Supports binary G-code"
msgstr "Supports binary G-code"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3838
msgid ""
"Enable, if the firmware supports binary G-code format (bgcode). To generate .bgcode files, make "
"sure you have binary G-code enabled in Configuration->Preferences->Other."
msgstr ""
"Enable, if the firmware supports binary G-code format (bgcode). To generate .bgcode files, make "
"sure you have binary G-code enabled in Configuration->Preferences->Other."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3844
msgid "How to apply limits"
msgstr "How to apply limits"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3845
msgid "Purpose of Machine Limits"
