msgid "Solid layers"
msgstr "Solid layers"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5084
msgid "Number of solid layers to generate on top and bottom surfaces."
msgstr "Number of solid layers to generate on top and bottom surfaces."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5090 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5091
msgid "Minimum thickness of a top / bottom shell"
msgstr "Minimum thickness of a top / bottom shell"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5097
msgid "Spiral vase"
msgstr "Spiral vase"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5098
msgid ""
"This feature will raise Z gradually while printing a single-walled object in order to remove any "
"visible seam. This option requires a single perimeter, no infill, no top solid layers and no "
"support material. You can still set any number of bottom solid layers as well as skirt/brim "
"loops. It won't work when printing more than one single object."
msgstr ""
"This feature will raise Z gradually while printing a single-walled object in order to remove any "
"visible seam. This option requires a single perimeter, no infill, no top solid layers and no "
"support material. You can still set any number of bottom solid layers as well as skirt/brim "
"loops. It won't work when printing more than one single object."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5107
msgid "Temperature variation"
msgstr "Temperature variation"

#. TRN PrintSettings : "Ooze prevention" > "Temperature variation"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5109
msgid ""
"Temperature difference to be applied when an extruder is not active. The value is not used when "
"'idle_temperature' in material settings is defined."
msgstr ""
"Temperature difference to be applied when an extruder is not active. The value is not used when "
"'idle_temperature' in material settings is defined."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5119
msgid "Emit temperature commands automatically"
msgstr "Emit temperature commands automatically"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5120
msgid ""
"When enabled, PrusaSlicer will check whether your custom Start G-Code contains G-codes to set "
"extruder, bed or chamber temperature (M104, M109, M140, M190, M141 and M191). If so, the "
"temperatures will not be emitted automatically so you're free to customize the order of heating "
"commands and other custom actions. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"PrusaSlicer settings, so you can put a \"M109 S[first_layer_temperature]\" command wherever you "
"want.\n"
"If your custom Start G-Code does NOT contain these G-codes, PrusaSlicer will execute the Start G-"
"Code after heated chamber was set to its temperature, bed reached its target temperature and "
"extruder just started heating.\n"
"\n"
"When disabled, PrusaSlicer will NOT emit commands to heat up extruder, bed or chamber, leaving "
"all to Custom Start G-Code."
msgstr ""
"When enabled, PrusaSlicer will check whether your custom Start G-Code contains G-codes to set "
"extruder, bed or chamber temperature (M104, M109, M140, M190, M141 and M191). If so, the "
"temperatures will not be emitted automatically so you're free to customize the order of heating "
"commands and other custom actions. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"PrusaSlicer settings, so you can put a \"M109 S[first_layer_temperature]\" command wherever you "
"want.\n"
"If your custom Start G-Code does NOT contain these G-codes, PrusaSlicer will execute the Start G-"
"Code after heated chamber was set to its temperature, bed reached its target temperature and "
"extruder just started heating.\n"
"\n"
"When disabled, PrusaSlicer will NOT emit commands to heat up extruder, bed or chamber, leaving "
"all to Custom Start G-Code."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5135
msgid "Force temperature integers"
msgstr "Force temperature integers"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5136
msgid ""
"When enabled, supported nozzle, bed and chamber temperature commands in generated and custom G-"
"code are rounded to whole numbers during export. This includes firmware-specific commands and "
"preview slider entries. Klipper always enforces integer temperatures. The original custom G-code "
"and slider entries remain unchanged."
msgstr ""
"When enabled, supported nozzle, bed and chamber temperature commands in generated and custom G-"
"code are rounded to whole numbers during export. This includes firmware-specific commands and "
"preview slider entries. Klipper always enforces integer temperatures. The original custom G-code "
"and slider entries remain unchanged."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5143
msgid "Custom printer parameters"
msgstr "Custom printer parameters"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5153
msgid ""
"This start procedure is inserted at the beginning, possibly prepended by temperature-changing "
"commands. See 'autoemit_temperature_commands'."
msgstr ""
"This start procedure is inserted at the beginning, possibly prepended by temperature-changing "
"commands. See 'autoemit_temperature_commands'."

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5162
msgid "Custom material parameters"
msgstr "Custom material parameters"

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5172
msgid ""
"This start procedure is inserted at the beginning, after any printer start gcode (and after any "
"toolchange to this material in case of multi-material printers). This is used to override "
"settings for a specific material. If PrusaSlicer detects M104, M109, M140 or M190 in your custom "
"codes, such commands will not be prepended automatically so you're free to customize the order of "
"heating commands and other custom actions. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"PrusaSlicer settings, so you can put a \"M109 S[first_layer_temperature]\" command wherever you "
"want. If you have multiple extruders, the gcode is processed in extruder order."
msgstr ""
"This start procedure is inserted at the beginning, after any printer start gcode (and after any "
"toolchange to this material in case of multi-material printers). This is used to override "
"settings for a specific material. If PrusaSlicer detects M104, M109, M140 or M190 in your custom "
"codes, such commands will not be prepended automatically so you're free to customize the order of "
"heating commands and other custom actions. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"PrusaSlicer settings, so you can put a \"M109 S[first_layer_temperature]\" command wherever you "
"want. If you have multiple extruders, the gcode is processed in extruder order."

